    "notes": "Served with the vcruz305 Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 DGX Spark recipe (github.com/vcruz305/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-EXL3-DGX-Spark-recipe at e0ebee8), native exllamav3 path. Engine: github.com/vcruz305/exllamav3 master at 329e051 (upstream v1.5.0 plus the fork's aarch64 guards and GB10 decode changes), built from source on the box with uv pip install --no-build-isolation -e . into a Python 3.12 venv with torch 2.13.0+cu130, triton 3.7.1, CUDA 13.0 (nvcc at /usr/local/cuda-13.0), TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST 12.1, GNU 13.3.0; driver 580.173.02, Ubuntu 24.04.4, kernel 6.17.0-1029-nvidia. Weights: turboderp/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-exl3 branch 3.05bpw_h5_ng5 at commit 69e33439ae950f17bcbe95c98f117d80f759ab6d, 85,139,442,313 bytes, sha256 of every LFS file checked against the Hub. The recipe's own headline path is examples/chat.py, which is a console chat, not a server; the recipe README names TabbyAPI as the OpenAI API layer for this engine, so the server is TabbyAPI (theroyallab/tabbyAPI main at 7208273) with a two-line patch that passes draft_model.draft_confidence to the Generator (stock TabbyAPI leaves it at the Generator default 0.4 and the recipe runs 0.6). TabbyAPI config: max_seq_len 262144, cache_size 262144, cache_mode 8,8, draft_mode mtp, draft_cache_mode 8,8, draft_num_tokens 5, dynamic_draft true, draft_confidence 0.6, chunk_size 2048, max_batch_size 4 (the TabbyAPI default for recurrent models), reasoning true with <think> and </think>, tool_format qwen3_coder, sysmem_recurrent_cache 4096 MB, sysmem_kv_cache 0. That is the recipe launcher scripts/exl3_native/tuning/run-qwen38-exl3.sh (chat.py -mode qwen35 -mtp -ndt 5 -dds -dc 0.6 -cq 8,8 -cs 262144) mapped onto TabbyAPI names, with the launcher environment EXL3_INT8_GEMV=0 EXL3_MOE_COOP_WIDE=1 EXL3_GR_INT8=1 EXL3_MTP_HEAD_N=65536 EXL3_NGRAM_STREAM=0, the process pinned with taskset -c 5-9,15-19 to the ten Cortex-X925 cores, and the pack's page cache dropped with the recipe's drop-model-cache.sh before load. Load took 59.3 s; after load the box had 97.4 GB of 121.6 GiB in use and 27.2 GB available, of which the server process held 36.5 GB resident on the host side (EXL3_NGRAM_STREAM=0 keeps the 32.6 GB n-gram table in system RAM). Every request here sets temperature 0 and seed 42, which is what the recipe measures with (greedy, -topk 1). The chat template defaults to thinking on with reasoning_effort xhigh; speed rows turn it off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false, eval rows use the template default unless a gotcha says otherwise."
  },
